      "prompt": "Why does a speed computed from count differences get coarser when the sample rate goes up?",
      "kind": "choice",
      "dimension": "C",
      "critical": false,
      "options": [
        "Faster sampling overloads the encoder so counts are lost.",
        "Shorter interval: one count is a bigger speed step.",
        "The gear ratio changes with the sample rate of the program.",
        "Higher sample rates add backlash in the gearbox."
      ],
      "answer": "1",
      "explanation": "The speed quantum is 2 pi / (N dt): halving dt doubles it.",
